+### Layout of the arrays
+
+By default, the arrays of a material data manager are stored point by
+point. They can also be stored component by component, which gives
+coalesced memory accesses on GPUs, by setting the `layout` member of an
+initializer:
+
+```python
+init = mgis_bv.MaterialDataManagerInitializer()
+init.layout = mgis_bv.FieldLayout.COMPONENT_BY_COMPONENT
+data2 = mgis_bv.MaterialDataManager(behaviour, ngauss, init)
+```
+
+The `gradients`, `thermodynamic_forces` and `internal_state_variables`
+members of the states, and the `K` member of the material data manager,
+are then still `numpy` arrays whose first dimension is the integration
+point, and whose strides account for the layout (see [this
+page](views.html)).
+
